-## v0.28.0: Correct the online Unlimited NOS clock
+## v0.29.0: Accept verified native car records in the tuner
+
+The S20 report exposed an incorrect assumption: active car data is not always heap-allocated. The native game also embeds it in its fixed racer-record array. The tuner now accepts those exact native slots **only when the current car, record kind, active record count, race table and ride pointer all agree**. Arbitrary low addresses remain rejected; the existing heap path and all other safety checks remain.
+
+Tests capture all 22 native slots and verify selected-preset-only Stage/Restore across all five modes, including the first and last slots. Native private preview/search matches heap-backed fixtures. The private evaluator permits writes only to the exact ride/curve regions, not neighboring racers or the rest of the copied image. No game save is performed by the extension.
+
+This fixes a proven rejection of valid native car storage. **The user's live capture has not yet been retested.** Reload with only v0.29 enabled, verify 0.29.0, then retry Load settings on the solo Performance Tuning main screen. If another check fails, retain its S-code or export the crash log; later layout protections have not been removed.
+
+The power panel also reports whether power fields were applied, are settling, or are blocked by a specific guard. Exported pace acknowledgement is separate from power application. These are observations, **not a measured speed increase**; no speed, power, driver or network setting is changed by this status addition.
+
+The final v0.29 suite passes **1,768 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations**. Independent checks cover all 22 native slots, selected Stage/Restore in all five presets, private write boundaries, and unchanged driving code. Power/pace confirmation also clears on stop, online opt-out, game exit, tuner suspension and replacement game sessions.
+
+The online NOS clock correction, working Street X behavior, Drift isolation, profiles, Drag protection and online collision/corner controls remain combined. No unrelated Drag lane candidate or unverified grip/downforce scaling is included. Live driving results and game-save persistence remain unverified.
+
+## Retained v0.28.0: Correct the online Unlimited NOS clock
 
 Unlimited NOS now refreshes an already-active NOS timestamp using the same clock the native game selected. The previous version always used the world clock; in an online fixture where the game's real clock was ahead, that made a full kit immediately appear depleted and caused repeated native stop/restart cycles. The corrected code retains the burst in that exact native test.
 
